=== Issues Found ===

[HIGH-1] BundleMgr.cpp, CertSourceMgr::DumpDuplicateCerts(), ~Line 665
  - BIO_get_mem_data() can return negative on error
  - Negative cast to size_t => SIZE_MAX-like value => buffer overflow in memcpy

[HIGH-2] CRLMgr.h getMfileSize()/setMfileSize() + CRLMgr.cpp ~Line 1121
  - getMfileSize() return type changed uint32_t->size_t in header
  - Caller 'uint32_t old_entire_sz = m_crl_sum->getMfileSize()' still truncates

[MEDIUM-3] CRLMgr.cpp NewFetch::createMmapCrlFile() ~Line 452
  - (uint32_t)SN_count*(uint32_t)sizeof(SerialNum) can overflow uint32_t for large CRLs

[MEDIUM-4] CRLMgr.cpp ReFetch::modifyMmapCrlFile() ~Line 1143
  - Same overflow pattern as MEDIUM-3 for new_SN_count

[MEDIUM-5] CRLMgr.cpp ReFetch::modifyMmapCrlFile() ~Line 1183
  - 'new_SN_count=%d' format specifier not updated; should be %u if unsigned

[MEDIUM-6] KeyMgmtDaemon.cpp downloadViaInternalProxyUrl() ~Line 437
  - Changed %lu to %ld for 'port'; if port is unsigned type %ld is incorrect

[MEDIUM-7] unittests/Makefile
  - KeyMgmtOpenSSLUtilTest.cpp added but commented out in TEST_SRCS as not implemented

[LOW-8] CRLMgr.h TcpBufferCrlQuery ~Line 247
  - Removed #pragma pack() - callers using sizeof(TcpBufferCrlQuery) should be verified

[LOW-9] CRLMgr.cpp timestamp_to_str() ~Line 231
  - No static_assert(sizeof(time_t)==8) to enforce 64-bit time_t assumption

=== Positive Changes ===
- memcpy() used instead of unaligned pointer casts (alignment safety fix)
- PRIu64/PRIx64 macros used throughout for uint64_t format strings
- #pragma pack(4) + sizeof assertion for SerialNum struct
- Bug fix: pos2==npos check added in get_csr_san()
- std::auto_ptr -> std::unique_ptr migration
- Comprehensive new unit test suites for Digicert/Godaddy/OpenSSL utilities
